#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290524 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096706 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8c990d69-54da-5541-948f-0d5eff96feb5" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the X-Intercepts of a Parabola Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "adec1f59-4414-5eba-a9d0-0be0539bcf76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289184}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "adec1f59-4414-5eba-a9d0-0be0539bcf76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289184} :answer-field/id #uuid "12a4955b-1b39-5914-8df2-241e9e148d62" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289773}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b992bd0f-c103-5e7d-8240-431930cfc4f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-240666" :question/problem "![](images/d4/d4c21d6ce09ff32004a28d18d223fef7858c377bccb0eb532cf2dda29a545f5e.png)\n\nThe value of the $x$-intercept of the parabola shown above is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the equation of the parabola. From the diagram, we see that the parabola has a vertex at $(-7,-2)$ and passes through the point $(-11,-6).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola with vertex $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(y-k)^{2}=4p(x-h).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $(h,k)=(-7,-2)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n(y+2)^{2}=4p(x+7).\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $(-11,-6),$ we substitute $x=-11$ and $y=-6$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-6+2)^{2} & =4p(-11+7) \\\\ (-4)^{2} & =4p\\cdot (-4) \\\\ 16 & =-16p \\\\ p & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+2)^{2} & =-4(x+7).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $x$-axis, we must have $y=0.$ So, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the parabola and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0+2)^{2} & =-4(x+7) \\\\ 4 & =-4(x+7) \\\\ -1 & =x+7 \\\\ x & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercept is $-8.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292537 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096708 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e182f71-db24-5c29-9c8b-2fc4b5ab5dd8" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Y-Intercepts of a Parabola Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b11eb3e0-5429-5dbf-9eb9-2fe0147cd44a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291404}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b11eb3e0-5429-5dbf-9eb9-2fe0147cd44a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291404} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7824f56-f0d4-5e6a-aab1-6508db9a964a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292343}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2ccfe5a9-f5ef-5f9b-aef4-c87ce64bd0db" :question/math-academy-id "q-251810" :question/problem "![](images/31/31618ee78ebe4834cf76aedebce7c25eca8413c6a4b9d91761ccc38dbd32b01d.png)\n\nThe value of the $y$-intercept of the parabola shown above  is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the equation of the parabola. From the diagram, we see that the parabola has a vertex at $(2,2)$ and passes through the point $(-2,-2).$\n\nThe general standard equation of an up- or down-opening parabola with vertex at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k),\n$$\n\nand substituting $(h,k)=(2,2)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n(x-2)^{2}=4p(y-2).\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $(-2,-2),$ we substitute $x=-2$ and $y=-2$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2-2)^{2} & =4p(-2-2) \\\\ 16 & =4p(-4) \\\\ p & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2} & =-4(y-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $y$-axis, we must have $x=0.$ So, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the parabola and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0-2)^{2} & =-4(y-2) \\\\ 4 & =-4(y-2) \\\\ -1 & =y-2 \\\\ y & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-intercept is $1.$"}]}
